#70202
"Corridor of Colored Clay"
"The small doorway to the south opens up into a large dusty loft, ill-lit by

several small chandeliers hanging low from the ceiling.  Not a drop of wax has

fallen upon the floor of dust-covered wooden boards, a few scattered

footprints marring the uniformity of the grey dust.  At the far end of the

loft there is a small window that does nothing to light the room.

"
"Though it is a loft, these rooms are called a corridor to make it seem

important and for alliteration's sake

