"Corridor of Colored Clay"
"Rows and rows of clay-molded statuettes, shaped like all mannor of strange and

mundane creatures, line the walls, each one painted differently.  Some of the

statuettes are so old that they hardly retain any of their original color,

while others are brighter and new.  Each is as well cared for as its neighbors

despite age, color, or form.  The shelves barely break to allow passage to an

easily ignorable door to the east which opens outwards, for it would not be

able to open inwards without hitting several of the shelves.

