#70225
"The Princess's Chamber"
"Each of the four corners of this room are piled with old, sometimes even

ancient, discarded toys, clothing, and books in no particular order.  A

small triangular window on the south wall looks out onto the battlements

below but is too small to get a good look at much of anything else nearby. 

The walls are covered with drawings and scribbled attempts at poetry in

many mediums, from charcoal to fading water paints.  A large chestnut bed

against the north wall takes up most of the space in the room.

"
